## Context

Author decision (2026-06-10): publish the reference as a standalone data
paper, but ONLY as a **strict, well-reconciled superset** of GEM, WRI and
Wikipedia. This is why it is blocked by 0498 (full per-plant GEM↔reference
HITL reconciliation): the superset claim must be earned per-plant, not
asserted. 0498 already frames the goal — "the reference contains every GEM
entry we judge a project — built, planned, and cancelled".

Strategic value (review §1): gives the reference a DOI and citable
identity independent of the technical report; pre-empts the
"single-author unaudited compilation" objection; each reuse = citation;
Paper B uses it as held-out validation object.

## What to do

1. After 0498 lands: extend the reconciliation to **WRI GPPD** and
   **Wikipedia** layers with the same per-plant HITL discipline
   (matcher-miss triage first, then compiler judgement per lead).
2. Produce the superset audit table: for each external-source entry,
   matched / added / excluded-with-reason. This table IS the data
   paper's core evidence.
3. Choose venue: Scientific Data descriptor vs Data in Brief (decide on
   length/effort budget at writing time).
4. Write the descriptor: collection method (PROVENANCE.md is the seed),
   scope boundary, per-cell provenance scheme, status vocabulary,
   validation (the audit table), reuse notes (PyPSA-VN,
   powerplantmatching ingestion).
5. Deposit dataset with DOI (Zenodo or journal-required repository),
   licence consistent with the repo (CC BY 4.0, per 0510).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Superset audit table generated from committed artifacts
- [ ] Every GEM/WRI/Wikipedia project entry accounted for
      (matched/added/excluded-with-reason)
- [ ] Descriptor manuscript drafted
- [ ] Dataset deposited with DOI
- [ ] Author sign-off on venue and submission

